// Down-air (light or heavy + down, in the air): a slow stomp below your feet.
// The clean hit is a "spike": it launches DOWNWARD (negative angle), so an
// opponent hit off the stage is sent toward the bottom blast zone. That's
// what makes edgeguarding (attacking someone trying to get back) worth it.
// On a grounded opponent it just pops them along the floor.
// Slow (7 startup) with big landing lag (14): risky to throw out carelessly.
